Material derived from MAME
==========================

No MAME source file is included in this repository. The following files
quote, change or restate specific MAME source files closely enough to
count as derived work (MAME release tags mame0285 and mame0289,
https://github.com/mamedev/mame):

  patches/mame/0001-ikari-cycle-interleave.patch
      quotes and changes lines of src/mame/snk/snk.cpp (mame0285)
      copyright-holders: Ernesto Corvi, Tim Lindquist, Carlos A. Lozano,
      Bryan McPhail, Jarek Parchanski, Nicola Salmoria, Tomasz Slanina,
      Phil Stroffolino, Acho A. Tang, Victor Trucco

  patches/mame/0002-m72-palette-from-ram-at-start.patch
      quotes and changes lines of src/mame/irem/m72_v.cpp (mame0285)
      copyright-holders: Nicola Salmoria

  patches/mame/0003-nec-rep-continuation-no-double-charge.patch
      quotes and changes lines of src/devices/cpu/nec/necinstr.hxx (mame0285)
      copyright-holders: Bryan McPhail

  tools/oracle/spang/kabuki.py (the Kabuki decryption as kabuki.cpp
  writes it: the two bit-pair swap functions, the byte decode and the key
  set of the Super Pang World set), and the same keys where
  docs/spang-hardware-spec.md lists them
      after src/mame/capcom/kabuki.cpp (mame0285)
      copyright-holders: Nicola Salmoria

  tools/oracle/arcade/z80steps.py reads src/devices/cpu/z80/z80.lst
  (mame0285) as data at run time; the step tables it prints or writes are
  derived from that file
      copyright-holders: Juergen Buchmueller, Andrei I. Holub

The documents under docs/ describe the behaviour of MAME drivers and
devices in their own words and cite MAME source files and line numbers;
they contain no MAME code beyond identifiers and single expressions.

